  "query_preview": "..\nA col located to the northeast will bring light to variable winds \nover the Marianas starting tonight, lifting north-northwest and \ndeparting the region by Saturday afternoon. A monsoon pattern that is\ncurrently south of the Marianas will move northward over Guam on \nFriday, bringing moderate to breezy southwest to west winds and a 40 \npercent chance of showers through the rest of the forecast period. \nThe CNMI can expect this regime starting Saturday afternoon, so light\nand variable winds and isolated showers are in store until then. \nIsland-effect showers are a possibility, but the size of these \nislands tend to be too small to cause substantial rainfall. The \nforecast zones were split into two to accommodate for the timing and\nspatial differences of the monsoon pattern. Isolated thunderstorms \nassociated with a typically wet monsoon pattern should not be ruled \nout by the end of the weekend and through next week.",
